/**
 * The three chart roles, and why there are three rather than the five
 * `ui-tokens.md` once listed.
 *
 *  - `chart1`     — the series colour: slot one of the categorical scale, and
 *                   the ONLY slot, because every chart on the platform is one
 *                   series (a bar per district, a bar per department). Slots
 *                   two onwards are chosen when a chart with two series exists,
 *                   by running the palette validator, not before. The theme hue
 *                   at L 0.59 light, the focus ring's step, because the fill's
 *                   own L 0.65 measures under 3:1 on the tertiary surface; this
 *                   one measures 3.23:1 there and 3.84:1 on `surface`. Dark
 *                   keeps L 0.68: 5.41:1 on the lightest dark surface.
 *  - `chartTrack` — the unfilled part of a bar or meter: a lighter step of the
 *                   SAME hue, so the whole length reads as one scale. It is
 *                   decorative (1.21:1 on `surface`); the value is always text.
 *  - `chartMuted` — de-emphasis. A bar a filter has set aside keeps its length
 *                   and loses its colour; its label keeps full contrast. Fading
 *                   the whole row, text included, is what this replaced.
 *
 * Status colours are NOT chart colours. A bar that means good or bad wears
 * `success`/`warning`/`danger` with an icon and a word; a bar that means "how
 * much" wears `chart1`.
 */

